% Text an ATS can read back out. T1 Computer Modern with no outline
% version installed is drawn as bitmap (Type 3) fonts, which carry no
% characters at all: "Experience" came back as "Exp erience" and
% "efficient" as "e\x1ecien t". Latin Modern is the same design in
% outline form; glyphtounicode then maps ligatures ("fi", "ffi") back
% to their letters. Guarded so a TeX without lmodern still compiles —
% the check read back from the PDF says when that happened.
\IfFileExists{lmodern.sty}{\usepackage{lmodern}}{}
\input{glyphtounicode}
\pdfgentounicode=1
